      "writtenOn": "2026-11-12T03:08:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "A few things:\n\n1. I doubt that component images intersecting the header are intended, however\n2. I doubt that Figure 4 there is normative, and\n3. The text for `ComponentLocationOffset` in Table 5 of DSP0267 v1.0.0 doesn\u0027t describe this constraint, which is where I would expect to find it\n\n\nI rather think we need some flags to control opinionated things like this.\n\nAs an aside, something I had in mind when writing the initial implementation of the parser was to have a flag that disallowed any intersection of components with other package elements (including other components). I didn\u0027t end up implementing the idea because I had already spent a lot of time on developing it as it was.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 12,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 13,
        "endChar": 54
      },
      "revId": "cafc790a1357acae58676a347451b309eff3bdde",
