      "writtenOn": "2026-11-12T13:10:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "DSP0267 v1.0.0 page 22,24:\n\n\u003e A firmware update package that complies with the structure and requirements within this clause shall be\nprovided to the UA for processing\n\n\u003e The firmware package payload contains the individual component images that can be transferred to the\nfirmware devices. \n\nAs per https://www.iso.org/sites/directives/current/part2/index.xhtml#_idTextAnchor212\n\n\u003e 16.2 Normative or informative?\nThe Terms and definitions clause is a normative element. It defines the way in which the listed terms shall be interpreted.\n\nAnd in the `Terms and Definitions Clause`\n\n\u003e 3.20 firmware update package\n\n\u003e a firmware package header describing the contents concatenated with one or more component images for one or more firmware devices\n\nMy interpretation here is that `concatenated` means they are back-to-back adjacent without padding or overlap and `contains` meaning there is no part of it that\u0027s outside the payload section.",
      "parentUuid": "d368fe74_45cd0156",
